{"id": "1aa6ca39-52f6-431b-9ccf-8cc72ecbc596", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T18:00:40.869260", "source": "user", "parent_id": "f0ba6459-c70b-4dba-8f34-db01ecfd2298", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"This is a design-only task: produce a final experimental design (rationale, controls, analysis plan, feasibility) for discovering causal relationships with unobserved common causes using the CAMUV algorithm. No execution is required, and no external compute/datasets are mandated by the brief (track.md confirms repositories and compute are not required; environment notes that successful exploratory commands do not constitute a completed experiment — do not present any such commands as proof of an executed experiment unless explicitly framed as illustrative script sketches under the design deliverable). Also note: I have not supplied reference materials, a paper, or source code for CAMUV; treat your working definition as an assumption that must be surfaced and justified, not as a confirmed fact about a specific paper/version. If you lack the algorithm's exact specification, propose a parameterized abstract model of CAMUV (inputs: observational data with candidate latent confounders, output: estimated causal graph / latent structure) and state this explicitly. Please return, at this stage, ONLY: (1) a brief inspection of any inputs you considered (repository state, available libraries, prior design notes — say so if none are relevant), (2) a proposed approach for the experiment design (graphical models, data-generating processes, conditions/configurations, baselines, metrics, controls, feasibility constraints), and (3) the consequential assumptions and uncertainties (CAMUV specification, assumptions on latent cardinality, identifiability, linearity/nonlinearity, noise regimes, sample sizes, evaluation protocol, and any unstated resource/runtime budget). Do not yet produce the full design document — wait for approach review before elaborating. If you need clarification on any of the above, ask in a focused way rather than fabricating specifics.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"How can you discover causal relationships in data with unobserved common causes using the CAMUV algorithm?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 24, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 1}
