ation.** Is the intended algorithm closer to Scheme A (augmented-variable search) or Scheme B (factor-residualization loop)? A single sentence / paper reference would let me ground the design.\\n- U2. **Variable type / cardinality.** Continuous only, discrete only, or both? Practical `p` range of interest (\\u2264 5, \\u2264 20, \\u2264 100, larger)?\\n- U3. **Latent cardinality range.** Is the interesting regime `K_true = 1\\u20132`, or do we need to handle `K_true \\u2265 3`?\\n- U4. **Functional regime.** Linear-Gaussian sufficient, or must nonlinear / discrete / mixed-type be first-class?\\n- U5. **Output type to evaluate.** DAG, MAG, PAG, or any? Determines primary metric choice.\\n- U6. **Real-data component.** Should the design include a real-world observational dataset (as an illustrative application), or remain synthetic-only? If real, I would need the dataset or its description.\\n- U7. **Budget envelope.** Any wall-clock / core-hour / disk budget if execution is later requested? Default proposal: \\u2264 200 single-core-hours total.\\n- U8. **Deliverable form.** Is the elaborated design expected as a markdown document only, or also accompanied by illustrative Python sketches? I default to **sketches clearly labeled illustrative**, per the environment note.\\n\\n### What I will *not* assume without confirmation\\n- That CAMUV corresponds to a specific named paper, version, or reference implementation \\u2014 I will not invent one.\\n- That any preinstalled library is usable \\\"as-is\\\"; the absence in this environment means each is either installed first or re-implemented.\\n- That CAMUV outperforms any specific baseline \\u2014 that is an empirical claim the *experiment* is meant to test, not a prior.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Next step.** Please confirm or amend any of A1\\u2013A6 and any of U1\\u2013U8 (especially U1 \\u2014 the CAMUV scheme). On approval, I will produce the full design document at `stage=result` with rationale, controls, analysis plan, feasibility, and audit-quality evidence from the repository inspection above.\", \"evidence\": \"Repository inspection: `/workspace` contains only `task.json`; `find -maxdepth 3` returned no other files. Decoded task.json confirms track.md inline text 'Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.' Environment probe: python3 --version reported 3.12.3 at /usr/bin/python3; explicit imports of numpy, scipy, networkx, sklearn, pandas, pgmpy, causalnex, castle, matplotlib each raised ModuleNotFoundError. Network disabled, GPU disabled, 24 CPU cores, no datasets supplied, bubblewrap runtime per public_task.environment. No reference paper, code, or design notes supplied for CAMUV \\u2014 abstract model proposed and explicitly flagged as an assumption rather than asserted as a specific known algorithm.\"}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-8bbc2556-ce91-470b-883b-3248c63bf8ff", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 14}
