{"id": "00e1ef94-1a09-436c-9a6c-bcb36a3697c6", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T18:03:32.292237", "source": "user", "parent_id": "7d9ab467-c26c-4a17-96aa-d95644765d62", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Approach approved with the following resolutions to your uncertainties, which you should record explicitly in the final design as locked assumptions rather than open questions. U1 (CAMUV specification): since no reference was supplied and this is design-only, proceed with the parameterized abstract model. Document BOTH CAMUV-A (augmented-variable search) and CAMUV-B (factor-residualization loop) in the design as two concrete instantiations of the same abstract procedure, with a labeled nomenclature (CAMUV-A, CAMUV-B) used consistently throughout the design document. Do not assert a specific paper, version, or reference implementation. A1-A6 stand as written with one amendment: A3 may keep K_max ≤ 3, but the regime map should at minimum cover K_true ∈ {0,1,2} and note the extension to K_true ≥ 3 as out-of-scope for the default battery (an 'extension cell' is acceptable if you flag identifiability caveats). U2: continuous variables only for the default battery; discrete/mixed-type explicitly out-of-scope, noted as a limitation. U3: K_true ∈ {0,1,2} is sufficient. U4: linear-Gaussian + nonlinear-additive as the two functional classes; post-nonlinear and discrete out-of-scope for the default. U5: report on the projected observational DAG (skeleton + orientation) as the primary output; treat FCI's PAG output as a secondary comparator only — do not mix metrics across output types without explicit conversion. U6: synthetic-only is acceptable; the regime map IS the answer. If you find a real-data illustration cheap to add without requiring external assets, you may include it as a clearly-labeled 'illustrative-only' appendix, but it is not required. U7: default budget ≤ 200 single-core-hours, ≤ 4 h wall-clock per cell, ≥ 100 seeds per cell — these are accepted. U8: deliver the full design as a single markdown document at a clear path under /workspace (e.g., /workspace/experiment_design.md), with illustrative Python sketches included inline but each prefixed with a header that explicitly marks them as 'ILLUSTRATIVE SKETCH — NOT EXECUTED', per the environment note that exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment. Required sections in the elaborated design, in this order: (1) Objective restatement & answer-shape (regime map). (2) Reference definition of CAMUV (both schemes, with pseudocode/skeleton, parameter table, hyperparameter grid). (3) DGP specification (SCM form, per-cell settings, ground-truth recording). (4) Factorial battery table. (5) Baselines and oracles with justification. (6) Metrics and primary/secondary designations. (7) Controls (negative, identifiability, sample-size, runtime). (8) Analysis plan (mixed-effects model, multiple-comparison correction, effect sizes + CIs). (9) Feasibility & resource estimate. (10) Assumptions & limitations (locked-in A1-A6, plus out-of-scope items from U2-U4). (11) Threats to validity & mitigations. (12) References/literature anchors (named only if you are citing well-known algorithms like PC, GES, FCI — do not fabricate CAMUV citations). Proceed to produce this document now.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"result\", \"approach_approved\": true}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 16}
