identifiability violations, metric comparability across DAG vs PAG outputs (locked U5), multiple comparisons, single-seed fragility on small n, latent-label non-identifiability at K_true >= 2, and wall-clock cliffs on oversize cells. CAMUV-A vs CAMUV-B conflation is addressed by reporting both side-by-side throughout and analyzing them as separate fixed-effect levels in the mixed model; the tertiary convergence-rate metric distinguishes scheme-specific failure modes.\\n\\nSection 12. References / literature anchors. Restricted to well-known algorithm classes: PC, GES, FCI, LV-PCMCI, linear-Gaussian factor models and PCA initialization, and ARI/NMI (Hubert and Arabie 1985). No CAMUV citation fabricated.\\n\\nAppendices. Appendix A is an optional real-data illustration placeholder, explicitly marked optional and not included. Appendix B is the headline deliverable checklist, restating that no experiment is claimed to have been executed.\\n\\nVerification. ls -la reports 23792 bytes. wc -l reports 418 lines. grep -c '^## ' reports 14. grep -nE '^## ' confirms the required section sequence. grep -c 'ILLUSTRATIVE SKETCH' reports 4 (three prefixed code blocks plus one prose mention). No experiment was executed and no scientific library was installed.\",\"evidence\":\"Repository state confirmed via ls and find at /workspace which contains only task.json. Decoded task.json contains inline documents.track.md text Design only task and repositories and compute are not required. Environment probe found python3 3.12.3 at /usr/bin/python3 with explicit imports of numpy, scipy, networkx, pandas, scikit-learn, pgmpy, causalnex, castle, matplotlib each raising ModuleNotFoundError. public_task.environment confirms network disabled, GPU disabled, 24 CPU cores, no datasets, bubblewrap runtime. The design document at /workspace/experiment_design.md was assembled in four sequential cat append chunks, each under the 12000-character shell-command limit. Verification at file write time prod